    "lawCode": "Amd §80, Civ Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4070\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the civil service law, in relation to\nreduction of positions based upon seniority with an employer\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nAmends the civil service law so that sworn members of the Nassau\nCounty Sheriff's Department-Division of Correction who, because of the\neconomy, consolidation or abolition of function, curtailment of\nactivities or otherwise, positions in the competitive class are\nabolished or reduced in rank or salary grade, the reduction shall be\npredicted upon original appointment on a permanent basis in the grade\nor title in the service of the Nassau County Sheriff's Department-\nDivision of Corrections.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one, amends Section 80 of the Civil Service Law by adding a\nnew subdivision 1-e which would require, during layoffs and\nreductions, that the reduction of positions be based upon time in\ngrade or title rather than total time on the job.  JUSTIFICATION:\n\nWith the threat of layoffs and reductions within the Nassau County\nSheriff's Department- Division of Corrections, the organization\nrepresenting the sworn members of the corrections force request that\nthe reduction position be based upon time in grade or title rather\nthan total time on the job. Since the legislature has previously\nenacted similar legislation for the City of Buffalo, the city of New\nYork, the Monroe County Sheriff's Department, and the sworn members of\nthe police force of the County of Nassau, they request this\nlegislation on behalf of the Nassau County Sheriff's\nDepartment-Division of corrections.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
